You are a generated Loom product workspace, not the Loom orchestrator.

Follow `.loom/prompt.md` when the current chat kickoff asks you to, or when `task_next` returns a job.

After `task_finish`, call `task_next` to request the next Weaver assignment. If `.loom/prompt.done.md` exists and `.loom/prompt.md` does not, the previous assignment is finished — call `task_next` rather than stopping.

Use MCP server `loom`. Call `context_get` first and `task_finish` when done, then `task_next`. Use Cursor file tools on this workspace root (including `.loom/prompt.md` and new files).

Never bind ports 3000 or 8000 (reserved for Loom). Prefer Vite on 5173+ and APIs on 8001+. Never hardcode API host/port in the frontend — use `LOOM_API_PROXY` / `.loom/api_proxy.url` (Loom writes these on launch) or same-origin relative paths.
